# RouterOS scripts are consumed by the router (and by netinstall-cli on Linux),
# not by Windows tooling. Git's autocrlf would hand them out with CRLF endings
# on this machine, which is a needless variable to introduce into a mechanism
# whose only trigger is a device wipe. Pin them to LF.
*.rsc text eol=lf

# Same reasoning: this runs on the Pi under bash. CRLF would break the shebang.
*.sh text eol=lf
